{
  "refused": false,
  "answer": "A Magistrate who believes an accusation was false and either frivolous or vexatious may first call on the complainant (or, if absent, issue a summons) to show cause why he should not pay compensation to the accused. The Magistrate must record any cause shown and, if satisfied, may order compensation not exceeding fifty thousand Taka (or twenty‑five thousand Taka for a Magistrate of the third class) to be paid by the complainant to the accused. If the payment is not made, the Magistrate may also order simple imprisonment of the complainant for up to thirty days.",
  "citations": [
    {
      "section": "250",
      "quote": "If in any case instituted upon complaint or upon information given to a police-officer or to a Magistrate, one or more persons is or are accused before a Magistrate or any offence triable by a Magistrate, and the Magistrate by whom the case is heard discharges or acquits all or any of the accused, and is or opinion that the accusation against them or any of them was false and either frivolous or vexatious, the Magistrate [shall], by his order of discharge or acquittal, if the person upon whose complaint or information the accusation was made is present, call upon him forthwith to show cause why he should not pay compensation to such accused or to each or any of such accused when there are more than one, or, if such person is not present direct the issue of a summons to him to appear and show cause as aforesaid."
    },
    {
      "section": "250",
      "quote": "The Magistrate shall record and consider any cause which such complainant or information may show and if he is satisfied that the accusation was false and either frivolous or vexatious [shall], for reasons to be recorded, direct that compensation to such amount not exceeding [fifty thousand Taka] or, if the Magistrate is a Magistrate of the third Class, not exceeding [twenty-five thousand Taka], as he may determine be paid by such complainant or informant to the accused or to each or any of them."
    },
    {
      "section": "250",
      "quote": "The Magistrate may, by the order directing payment of the compensation under sub-section (2), further order that, in default of payment, the person ordered to pay such compensation shall suffer simple imprisonment for a period not exceeding thirty days."
    }
  ]
}

